# Security headers for quietkeep.pages.dev — Doctrine §16.6
#
# Unlike the hub, Quietkeep carries NO inline script or style: index.html loads
# one external module (app.js) and one stylesheet, and the UI builds DOM with
# textContent, never innerHTML. That means a STRICT Content-Security-Policy is
# achievable here, and it lands now — before /capture?text= gives the app a
# public input surface a hostile link can reach.
#
# The CSP is verified, not hoped: tools/serve.mjs applies this file's headers to
# every response, so smoke.mjs and a11y.mjs already exercise the app UNDER this
# policy, and smoke fails on any console error — a CSP violation is a console
# error. A policy nobody ran the app under is the V-10 shape.
#
# No Strict-Transport-Security: pages.dev is HTTPS-only and Cloudflare owns TLS;
# a header with lock-in semantics that cannot be tested from here is left to the
# platform.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
